 "summary": "Each new declaration sits in its natural home: the GL\u2082-specific class-function extensionality principle gets its own `GL2/ClassFunction.lean` (it cannot live in the generic `CharacterTable/ClassFunction.lean` or in `LinearAlgebra/.../NormalForm.lean` without crossing topic boundaries), the elliptic induced representation joins the existing `EllipticInduction.lean` mirroring the layer `ScalarUnipotentInduction.lean` already carries, and `Cuspidal.lean` sits beside the other GL\u2082 rows. All imports resolve to used declarations (`FDRep.ofLinearCharacter`, `finrank_indFDRep_ofLinearCharacter`, `indClassFun_ofFDRep_character`, `virtualCharacters`, `character_mem_virtualCharacters`, `FiniteField.pow_natCard_pow_natCard`) and none is a broad `import Mathlib`; no `Foo`/`FooBar` sibling pair is introduced in `GL2/`.",
